Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · TypeScript strict · Tailwind v4 ·
CSS Modules · Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Storage) · Drizzle ORM · Dexie ·
Vercel AI SDK · Zod · Vitest · Playwright · pnpm workspaces.

No turbo. No Capacitor in this repository; native lives in `../kayamo-mobile`.

Tailwind is effectively preflight plus `@theme` tokens for the shared primitives
in `@kayamo/ui`. Route styling is CSS Modules over the Liquid Glass layer. Do not
reach for utility classes in new route code.

Do not substitute a library without asking.

Commands: `pnpm dev` (port 3002), `pnpm build`, `pnpm test`, `pnpm typecheck`,
`pnpm lint`, `pnpm test:e2e`, `pnpm test:security`, `pnpm ph-core:build`.

- Server Components by default; "use client" only where interaction requires it.
- Route handlers validate input with Zod at the boundary, authenticate before
  doing work, and set `private, no-store` on authenticated responses.
- Migrations are hand-written SQL under `supabase/migrations/`, reviewed and
  committed, then applied with the Supabase CLI — never ad hoc. Record what was
  applied in `docs/releases/`.
- Add a dependency to the package that uses it, not to the root.
- `next build` uses webpack; `next dev` uses Turbopack. They disagree — notably
  on CSS Modules. A green dev server is not evidence that the build passes.
